terminal-text

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Draw text as a macOS terminal does: a tape font keeps the embedded fallbacks and finds its bold face, fallback glyphs take the primary font's height, symbols no bundled face has come from system fonts, a one-cell symbol prefers a text face to the emoji face, SVG text stays on its cells in browsers, box glyphs stay in their cells, and the pointer scales with the font.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream evp matches a terminal's glyph fallback, sizing and cell placement in GIF and SVG output, such as after its backup-font scaling fix 15011a9 covers these cases.
